{
  "name": "two_flat_racks_draft",
  "title": "Two 20 ft flat racks: one KR 210 on rack b sets rails and modules across the gap, two KR 20 on rack a drive the bolts and the pins, the tube worked in three stages",
  "summary": "Draft of the second direction, not yet a design that passes its checks. The cell stands on two 20 ft flat racks set down side by side with a nominal gap of 25 mm. The holder, the tube and two KUKA KR 20 R1810-2 on short tracks stand on rack a; one KUKA KR 210 R2700-2 on a track stands on rack b, with the pallet and the rail rack outside the +X side beyond it. The 10.6 m tube is longer than a rack and is worked in three stages that move it toward -Y between stages: rails 0-3 and modules 0-2, rails 4-6 and modules 3-5, rails 7-9 and modules 6-8. A bare tube comes in over the +Y end and a finished bay leaves over the -Y end.",
